Gears of War 3: startup shader loading progress. The pipeline cache reports the number of stored
pipelines it builds at startup and each one created (rex/shader_progress.h, in rexruntime so every
module shares it), and rexruntime exports rex_shader_loading_set_active / rex_shader_loading_get
for the host app. The game's own src/sdk/rex_app.cpp (ReXApp is compiled into the game exe, not
the runtime) runs that build off the UI thread behind a "Compiling shaders  done / total" panel,
instead of a black "Not responding" window. For testing, dxbc_cache_bust (a nonzero number)
changes every shader's generator name, so the bytes differ but not the code and the driver's own
shader cache misses.

diff --git a/include/rex/shader_progress.h b/include/rex/shader_progress.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e26f4b9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/rex/shader_progress.h
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+// Gears of War 3 recomp: startup shader loading progress, for the loading screen. The host app marks the
+// loading active while the GPU plugin builds the stored shaders and pipelines; the plugin sets the
+// pipeline count and advances it as each one is created (0 / 0 while it still reads and
+// translates the shaders). Lives in rexruntime so both DLLs see the same counters.
+#pragma once
+
+#include <cstdint>
+
+namespace rex {
+
+struct ShaderLoadingProgress {
+  bool active = false;
+  uint32_t done = 0;
+  uint32_t total = 0;
+};
+
+void SetShaderLoadingActive(bool active);
+void SetShaderLoadingTotal(uint32_t total);
+// Counts one created pipeline while the loading is active.
+void AdvanceShaderLoading();
+ShaderLoadingProgress GetShaderLoadingProgress();
+
+}  // namespace rex
